    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Show that $y=x^2\\sqrt{x}$ can be written as $y=x^{5/2}$, then show that the derivative is $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{5}{2}x\\sqrt{x}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=x^{5/2}$ and $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{5}{2}x\\sqrt{x}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=x^2\\times x^{1/2}\\\\y&=x^{2+1/2}\\\\y&=x^{5/2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{5}{2}x^{3/2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{5}{2}x^1\\times x^{1/2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{5}{2}x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
